# Root Dockerfile does `COPY . .` — anything here still ends up in every API
# image layer regardless of how the build context got onto disk (rsync
# excludes only protect the transfer, not a `COPY .` that already has the
# files locally). Filled in 2026-08-13 after apps/pos-native's Xcode
# simulator build artifacts (2.2GB, StripeTerminal.framework debug build)
# had been sitting in the VPS build context from an earlier, non-excluding
# rsync and filled the disk mid-deploy — same 2.2GB, same layer, copied into
# both the suite-api and stock-api images every single build.

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
build
.vite
*.tsbuildinfo
.git
# Env files at ANY depth: these now carry wallet private keys and Stripe
# secrets on dev machines, and `COPY . .` would bake them into every image
# layer. The .example files are covered too — nothing reads them at runtime.
.env
.env.local
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.log
firepit-log.txt
coverage
.firebase
.playwright-cli
output
tmp
*.bak
.pnpm-store
packages/db/generated
.prisma

# Never needed by any backend container — an Expo/React Native iOS shell,
# and its ios/build directory alone can run into gigabytes of simulator
# framework artifacts.
apps/pos-native
